Package: stormbreaker
Title: Transcriptomic Prediction and Model Comparison
Version: 0.3.47
Authors@R: 
    person(
      given = "HimejimaGyomei",
      role = c("aut", "cre"),
      email = "Polishedtjq1171137951@outlook.com"
    )
Description: Build and compare transcriptomic prediction models for binary
    and right-censored survival outcomes. A common interface combines model
    specification, feature selection, shared-fold comparison, nested tuning,
    final fitting and independent-cohort evaluation. Saved predictions support
    discrimination, calibration, decision-curve analysis, feature stability,
    cohort-level synthesis and graphical reports. Reusing identical fold-local
    forest selections accelerates comparisons across multiple learners. Models
    are provided through native R engines with task-specific configurations.
    Native multiclass forests, multinomial regularized regression,
    discriminant analysis, naive Bayes and classification trees support
    independent feature analysis and shared-fold model evaluation.
